<title>BELGIUM: GIB CEO says share not overvalued-paper.</title>
<headline>GIB CEO says share not overvalued-paper.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>GIB chief executive officer Diego du Monceau is frustrated with the company's share price, newspaper Wall Street Journal Europe said in an interview published on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't think it (the share) is overvalued,&quot; du Monceau told the newspaper.</p>
<p>Monceau also confirmed the company was looking for a buyer for its department store division, Inno, the Wall Street Journal said. &quot;We have two core businesses today...,&quot; du Monceau said, referring to food retailing and do-it-yourself stores.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
